php-ext-xz (XZ compression support for PHP)

php-ext-xz is a PHP extension providing XZ (LZMA2) compression and
decompression functions.

By default, the xz extension is enabled in "/etc/php.d/xz.ini". If you
want to disable it without removing this package, you can comment out
the "extension=xz" line. If you do this, reinstalling the package will
not re-enable the extension (your xz.ini is preserved).

To check whether the extension is loaded, you can run this from the
shell:

  $ php -r 'var_dump(extension_loaded("xz"));'

...if you see "bool(true)", it's loaded.

If you intend to permanently remove php-ext-xz, you should delete
its config file afterwards:

  # removepkg php-ext-xz
  # rm -f /etc/php.d/xz.ini

If you use PHP with Apache's mod_php, you'll have to restart Apache
after installing this, for PHP scripts to see the extension. E.g.:

  # /etc/rc.d/rc.httpd restart

The same is true of PHP FastCGI (FPM), if you use it:

  # /etc/rc.d/rc.php-fpm restart
